.Dd October 2, 2026
.Dt GETRUSAGE 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm getrusage
.Nd get resource usage
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/resource.h
.Ft int
.Fn getrusage "int who" "struct rusage *usage"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn getrusage
stores in
.Fa usage
the resources used by
.Fa who :
.Bl -tag -width "RUSAGE_CHILDREN"
.It Dv RUSAGE_SELF
The calling process: all its threads, those that have ended included.
.It Dv RUSAGE_THREAD
The calling thread.
.It Dv RUSAGE_CHILDREN
The children the caller's process has reaped with
.Xr wait 2 ,
each with the children it reaped itself.
.El
.Pp
.Va ru_utime
and
.Va ru_stime
are the CPU time the timer charged in user mode and in the kernel, the
ticks
.Xr times 2
reports, as seconds and microseconds.
.Pp
.Va ru_maxrss
is the most memory the process had in use, in kilobytes: the larger of
the resident size of its address space and of each earlier one, as it
ended at an
.Xr execve 2 ,
or for
.Dv RUSAGE_CHILDREN
the most any reaped child reported.
For
.Dv RUSAGE_THREAD
it is the process's.
Linux records the peak at each page fault; this kernel measures an
address space when it is asked and when it ends, so a process that freed
memory before either reports less than Linux would.
The kernel keeps no other resource count, so the thirteen counters after
.Va ru_maxrss
are zero.
.Ss System call interface
The i386 system call number is 77.
EBX contains
.Fa who
and ECX points to the 72-byte i386 structure: two timevals of 32-bit
seconds and microseconds, then fourteen 32-bit counters.
musl and glibc convert it to their structure with 64-bit seconds.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn getrusage
returns 0 on success, or -1 on failure and sets
.Va errno .
The kernel returns the negative error number.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The default suite's
.Pa tests/musl/cputimemusl.c
checks that the usage of the process and of its thread is what
.Fn times
reports, and that the children's usage rises by what
.Xr wait4 2
reported for a child it reaped.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width "[EFAULT]"
.It Bq Er EFAULT
.Fa usage
cannot be written.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
.Fa who
is none of the three.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr gettimeofday 2 ,
.Xr wait 2 ,
.Xr proc 5
